  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "If $(a-b)^2+10ab=120$, find the maximum possible value of $ab$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$12$, attained when $a=b=\\sqrt{12}$ or $a=b=-\\sqrt{12}$.\n\nSince $(a-b)^2\\geq0$, we have $10ab\\leq120$.",
      "worked": "Since $(a-b)^2\\geq0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}10ab&=120-(a-b)^2\\\\10ab&\\leq120\\\\ab&\\leq12.\\end{align*}$$\nEquality holds when $a=b$. Taking $a=b=\\sqrt{12}$ satisfies the given equation and gives $ab=12$. Hence the maximum possible value is $12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
